WEBVTT

00:18.910 --> 00:20.610
Good morning.

00:20.610 --> 00:24.070
Good morning. We're depending on you.

00:26.190 --> 00:28.920
He will be helping us with this job.

00:28.920 --> 00:31.670
I am Marten Liebert 
from the Remerio Trading Company.

00:32.430 --> 00:35.020
My name is Nora Arendt.

00:35.020 --> 00:37.470
Then, let us depart immediately.

00:37.470 --> 00:38.300
Yes.

00:42.260 --> 00:45.100
Then, please follow me.

00:49.090 --> 00:51.010
Will things go smoothly?

00:54.510 --> 00:59.950
If it doesn't, we will only have 
dark days ahead.

01:06.420 --> 01:10.640
Spice and Wolf

01:10.640 --> 01:11.760
Spice and Wolf

01:11.760 --> 01:17.100
Spice and Wolf

02:36.370 --> 02:38.850
Let's settle down around here today.

02:37.170 --> 02:42.180
<b>Episode 11
Forest of Wolves and Frigid Rain</b>

02:39.510 --> 02:44.050
What are you saying so leisurely?! 
The sun has yet to set!

02:44.050 --> 02:45.180
U-Um...

02:45.180 --> 02:47.490
We must hurry as quickly as possible!

02:50.430 --> 02:53.440
Then, you may move forward on your own.

02:53.720 --> 02:56.690
Hungry wolves will be waiting for you.

02:57.850 --> 03:03.330
Shepherds must rest early in order to 
guard the sheep from attacks in the night.

03:03.830 --> 03:08.330
The safety of the sheep 
is a priority for this endeavor.

03:08.330 --> 03:12.420
That's why following Ms. Nora's words 
is in our best interests.

03:14.610 --> 03:15.920
My apologies.

03:16.980 --> 03:19.820
My nerves keep telling me to move quickly.

03:19.820 --> 03:22.430
Of course, the entire trading company 
is on your shoulders.

03:22.430 --> 03:24.900
We will enter the dangerous forest tomorrow.

03:24.900 --> 03:27.010
We should rest well tonight.

03:32.330 --> 03:35.400
It feels like anything could show up in there.

03:35.400 --> 03:37.900
Please don't panic even if any wolves appear.

03:37.900 --> 03:40.650
I will definitely make sure 
you make it to town.

03:40.650 --> 03:42.140
We're depending on you.

03:46.330 --> 03:48.990
May the grace of God be with us.

03:58.020 --> 04:01.610
Do you think things will go 
smoothly with the wolves?

04:01.610 --> 04:03.760
No. We are already surrounded.

04:03.760 --> 04:04.590
Huh?!

04:04.590 --> 04:08.850
Even <i>if</i> such a thing happens, 
I will guarantee your safety.

04:10.310 --> 04:13.370
However, I cannot make promises 
about everyone else.

04:13.370 --> 04:15.980
Everyone needs to make it 
through this safely...

04:16.730 --> 04:19.070
I truly do not know the outcome.

04:19.370 --> 04:21.480
Right now, the forest is downwind from us.

04:21.480 --> 04:22.700
If there are wolves,

04:22.700 --> 04:26.570
they will have noticed the sheep and are 
sharpening their fangs as we speak...

04:32.620 --> 04:34.560
What a clever dog.

04:34.560 --> 04:37.460
That dog has already realized what I am.

04:37.460 --> 04:38.630
Is that so?

04:38.630 --> 04:42.420
He has been keeping an eye on me 
since the moment we met.

04:42.810 --> 04:44.630
His eyes clearly convey his intention.

04:44.630 --> 04:49.140
"If you lay your hands on the sheep, 
I will tear at your throat."

04:49.420 --> 04:53.690
But, well, I am the Wise Wolf Holo.

04:53.690 --> 04:56.510
I will not respond to the threats 
of a mere dog.

04:56.870 --> 04:59.170
Do you think Nora has realized it?

05:00.070 --> 05:04.160
If this smuggling operation fails, 
Nora will be the one in the most danger.

05:04.160 --> 05:07.400
As long as we keep our mouths shut, 
there's a chance that we can escape.

05:07.400 --> 05:10.120
However, Nora has no excuse.

05:10.520 --> 05:13.930
You really are too sweet to that girl.

05:13.930 --> 05:17.330
I've already told you the punishment 
that's waiting if we get caught.

05:19.360 --> 05:21.710
I don't think she can withstand 
something like that.

05:22.050 --> 05:25.880
Then, just protect her 
so such a thing does not happen.

05:42.740 --> 05:48.650
According to Nora, we'll reach Lamtra 
by afternoon, if we depart at dawn.

05:48.650 --> 05:51.740
Then, my work will begin after that.

05:52.080 --> 05:55.860
I will rest well so I do not make 
any mistakes in the negotiations.

05:56.750 --> 05:58.010
Sweet dreams.

05:59.330 --> 06:00.080
Oops.

06:26.530 --> 06:27.820
Please wake up!

06:29.320 --> 06:30.400
What is going on?!

06:30.400 --> 06:31.240
Stand back!

07:14.530 --> 07:16.540
Have they been driven off?

07:16.540 --> 07:20.500
I'm not sure, but they have 
distanced themselves.

07:20.500 --> 07:23.040
The wolves here are always like this.

07:23.040 --> 07:27.050
I rarely hear them howl, and
they rarely show signs of attacking.

07:27.050 --> 07:30.000
They just watch us the entire time.

07:30.000 --> 07:33.140
It is very strange that they do not howl.

07:34.430 --> 07:37.630
There may be something other than wolves here.

07:37.630 --> 07:42.100
For instance, monsters borne 
from the corpses of travelers.

07:45.650 --> 07:47.420
Holo, that's enough...

07:47.420 --> 07:48.980
I am half-serious.

07:48.980 --> 07:49.690
Huh?

08:10.380 --> 08:12.130
Now, it is my turn.

08:15.420 --> 08:17.340
I hope things go well.

08:17.340 --> 08:18.310
Me, too.

08:24.630 --> 08:28.150
U-Um! Ms. Holo...

08:28.420 --> 08:30.780
Are you knowledgeable about wolves?

08:31.840 --> 08:32.800
Hm?

08:32.800 --> 08:34.030
No! Um...

08:34.030 --> 08:38.910
You noticed the wolves 
extremely quickly last night...

08:40.130 --> 08:41.820
It was a coincidence.

08:41.820 --> 08:43.910
Is that so?

08:45.390 --> 08:49.920
To begin with, the men with us 
are too undependable.

08:51.210 --> 08:52.920
Do you not agree?

08:52.920 --> 08:55.860
Huh? Oh, I-I wouldn't say that.

08:55.860 --> 08:58.700
Then, does that really look dependable to you?

08:58.700 --> 09:00.600
W-Well...

09:02.790 --> 09:05.180
Do not hold back. Speak.

09:12.530 --> 09:15.820
It seems you are a good judge of character.

09:19.530 --> 09:24.460
To begin with, I am traveling alone with a man.

09:24.460 --> 09:28.980
It is strange to even ask whether or not 
I am knowledgeable of wolves.

09:28.980 --> 09:30.650
What do you mean?

09:31.550 --> 09:34.980
A wolf appears every night.

09:34.980 --> 09:38.550
After all, such a cute rabbit 
is sitting right before it.

09:38.550 --> 09:43.930
How can a rabbit that is hunted by a wolf 
every night not know of wolves?

09:44.610 --> 09:47.560
U-Um, y-you mean...

09:49.710 --> 09:53.190
Well, he is more like 
the rabbit in our situation.

09:53.450 --> 09:56.620
If I do not care for him, 
he will die of loneliness.

10:00.200 --> 10:07.660
That is why it is a "coincidence" that
I noticed the wolves so early last night.

10:07.660 --> 10:12.200
I thought you might be a shepherd, Ms. Holo.

10:12.200 --> 10:13.750
Oh? Why ever so?

10:14.020 --> 10:18.180
It seems that Enek is 
very attentive to you, Ms. Holo.

10:19.380 --> 10:23.640
Hm, that is easy to understand. 
He must be smitten by me.

10:23.950 --> 10:24.620
Huh?

10:25.240 --> 10:28.480
Oh, um... You mean, Enek is?

10:28.480 --> 10:31.960
It is because you treasure him so dearly.

10:31.960 --> 10:35.220
He probably thinks your affection 
for him is unchanging.

10:35.220 --> 10:40.340
That is why he grows greedy 
and occasionally flirts with others.

10:40.340 --> 10:44.280
You must sometimes 
show your cold side to a man.

10:44.280 --> 10:46.700
That is how to keep him in line.

10:46.700 --> 10:51.740
I will do as you say if he cheats on me again.

10:51.740 --> 10:55.380
However, I want to praise him 
as much as I can right now.

10:55.380 --> 10:59.220
Whether this job is a success or a failure,

10:59.220 --> 11:02.590
I will probably quit being a shepherd.

11:05.790 --> 11:07.600
It is exactly as I have said!

11:13.430 --> 11:15.070
You're absolutely right...

11:29.590 --> 11:30.700
How did things go?

11:33.490 --> 11:34.500
As you can see.

11:35.630 --> 11:37.140
How amazing!

11:41.060 --> 11:42.850
Now, we just need to bring this back.

11:42.850 --> 11:47.100
Let us find a suitable time to feed them 
the nuggets and pass through the city gates.

11:48.330 --> 11:49.390
Yes.

11:49.390 --> 11:52.000
The sun is already setting today.

11:52.000 --> 11:55.930
We should camp near the forest 
and pass through it tomorrow.

11:55.930 --> 11:57.230
I agree.

12:00.220 --> 12:02.450
The rain is coming...

12:21.380 --> 12:23.360
Shit! They're catching up to us!

12:23.360 --> 12:24.370
No.

12:24.370 --> 12:25.720
We have already been surrounded.

12:25.720 --> 12:26.340
What?!

12:28.100 --> 12:29.290
Enek!

12:38.190 --> 12:40.320
Shit! Shit!

12:44.470 --> 12:45.410
Enek!

13:00.380 --> 13:03.590
As I thought, that girl is quite skilled.

13:04.290 --> 13:08.720
Wolves surround their prey 
and hunt them with caution and cunning.

13:09.210 --> 13:13.310
She is well aware of that 
and gives her orders perspicaciously.

13:13.310 --> 13:18.940
Also, this long formation makes it difficult 
for the wolves to make a move.

13:18.940 --> 13:20.970
Then, are we all right?

13:21.420 --> 13:24.690
No. It is only a matter of time 
in this terrible weather.

13:27.900 --> 13:28.660
Enek!

13:37.370 --> 13:38.460
Mr. Lawrence!

13:45.690 --> 13:46.630
Stay back!

14:02.670 --> 14:06.140
Even humans say, "Young ones these days."

14:06.140 --> 14:06.900
Huh?

14:07.450 --> 14:10.710
You should have that girl and boy go on ahead.

14:11.230 --> 14:13.990
After that, you should 
separate from me as well.

14:13.990 --> 14:15.500
What are you saying so suddenly?

14:42.990 --> 14:44.740
Wh-What was that?!

14:44.740 --> 14:48.070
The wolf in this forest is no normal wolf.

14:48.070 --> 14:50.660
Their target is not the sheep.

14:50.660 --> 14:51.410
What?!

14:57.850 --> 14:59.500
Cheap stubbornness.

14:59.500 --> 15:01.110
Crude pride.

15:02.150 --> 15:04.780
They are things that young ones hold dear.

15:05.610 --> 15:09.070
I must take care of them myself.

15:09.650 --> 15:12.760
Look, no one will move 
until you give them orders.

15:13.150 --> 15:15.220
You are my partner.

15:19.410 --> 15:21.600
We will take care of things here!

15:23.730 --> 15:26.620
Please go on ahead as planned!

15:26.620 --> 15:28.020
No way!

15:29.030 --> 15:30.490
Mr. Lawrence!

15:30.490 --> 15:32.360
Let's go, Ms. Nora.

15:32.700 --> 15:35.330
This will all be for naught if 
we are hunted down by the wolves.

15:36.990 --> 15:39.290
We will meet you near the walls of Ruvinheigen!

15:39.290 --> 15:41.960
Then, we shall all become rich together!

15:42.250 --> 15:43.630
I wish you luck!

15:54.290 --> 15:56.920
You should get away from me as well.

15:56.920 --> 15:59.520
It will be troublesome for me 
if you are too close.

16:00.370 --> 16:02.270
You understand, do you not?

16:03.730 --> 16:05.440
I won't forgive you if you lose.

16:08.770 --> 16:13.580
If you were a handsome male, 
I would kiss you at this moment.

16:16.700 --> 16:17.910
Oh, that's right.

16:17.910 --> 16:20.100
Keep this safe for me.

16:20.100 --> 16:21.750
Y-Yeah...

16:26.930 --> 16:31.380
I hope to settle this peacefully, 
but I am not sure what will happen.

16:31.720 --> 16:34.080
It will be cold if I am naked 
when we rejoin them.

16:34.080 --> 16:35.750
Will that not also cause you trouble?

16:40.420 --> 16:41.350
I'll see you again.

17:07.190 --> 17:09.960
The wolves are no longer chasing us.

17:11.700 --> 17:14.050
It seems we managed to escape.

17:14.050 --> 17:16.220
Mr. Lawrence and Ms. Holo 
haven't caught up with us.

17:16.660 --> 17:18.090
Let us hurry ahead.

17:18.090 --> 17:20.470
We cannot let their deaths be in vain.

17:20.470 --> 17:22.270
Deaths? Please don't say such things!

17:23.910 --> 17:25.230
My apologies.

17:25.740 --> 17:30.860
But if we stay here, their courageous 
decision will be for naught.

17:31.250 --> 17:32.580
Now, let's go.

18:09.170 --> 18:11.440
Is that all you have to say for yourself?

18:17.460 --> 18:19.610
As I thought, you are too young.

18:22.100 --> 18:26.540
Your attitude toward your elders is lacking.

18:35.910 --> 18:36.670
Holo...

18:37.490 --> 18:38.780
I hope you're all right.

18:42.740 --> 18:44.430
I'm so powerless...

18:47.620 --> 18:48.540
Holo!

18:52.820 --> 18:54.220
Mr. Lawrence?

18:54.220 --> 18:56.150
Oh. Y-Yes!

18:56.150 --> 18:58.100
Thank goodness you're safe.

18:58.100 --> 18:59.170
Yes...

18:59.170 --> 19:03.240
We couldn't stand still after hearing 
about the situation from Mr. Liebert.

19:03.690 --> 19:07.290
We were on stand-by 
outside the forest, just in case.

19:07.700 --> 19:09.370
I see.

19:09.370 --> 19:12.200
So, Mr. Lawrence. Where are your things?

19:12.200 --> 19:13.130
Huh?

19:13.130 --> 19:16.750
Oh, over there, with my horse.

19:16.750 --> 19:20.730
I see. We should take cover 
from the rain first.

19:27.490 --> 19:30.890
Um, Mr. Lawrence, where is your companion?

19:34.190 --> 19:35.740
She isn't with me.

19:35.740 --> 19:37.370
That's good to hear.

19:37.370 --> 19:37.860
Huh?

19:45.130 --> 19:46.180
What are you doing?!

19:46.180 --> 19:48.370
We wouldn't blame you
 for thinking poorly of us.

19:48.370 --> 19:50.570
Remerio Trading is betraying us?!

19:50.570 --> 19:52.310
It's just for insurance.

19:52.310 --> 19:54.240
We're teetering at the edge 
of a cliff ourselves.

19:54.240 --> 19:57.270
We need to eliminate all the dangers we can!

19:58.570 --> 20:02.460
We were a bit reluctant 
since you had a woman with you.

20:02.460 --> 20:04.650
But it's good to hear she isn't with you.

20:04.650 --> 20:07.340
We'll let you keep your companion's memento.

20:08.690 --> 20:13.600
It's not as though it doesn't pain us
 to be unable to say, "Let's meet again."

20:15.780 --> 20:19.980
It depresses me to think of 
what we have to do next.

20:19.980 --> 20:22.210
She's a woman, after all...

20:22.210 --> 20:23.240
Hey! Hold your tongue!

20:23.240 --> 20:24.030
You can't be serious!

20:25.070 --> 20:26.810
Be quiet!

20:28.510 --> 20:30.430
Don't you dare lay a hand on her!

20:35.290 --> 20:36.780
Bastard!

20:40.090 --> 20:44.590
Just lie there and become food for the wolves!

20:47.990 --> 20:53.220
Hey, why don't we tie up the girl 
and leave her behind like this, too?

20:53.220 --> 20:55.380
Then the wolves will take care of her.

20:55.380 --> 20:56.730
Don't be stupid!

20:56.730 --> 21:01.840
She's able to escape this forest 
without losing a single sheep.

21:01.840 --> 21:04.320
We don't know what kind of 
pagan sorcery she has!

21:04.320 --> 21:09.450
Even if we tie her up, blindfold her, 
and leave her here, she will probably survive.

21:09.450 --> 21:12.190
Then we'll be the ones who meet a terrible end.

21:12.690 --> 21:13.870
That's true.

21:14.210 --> 21:16.320
Even so, my heart is heavy.

21:16.320 --> 21:20.910
I won't be able to eat for a while 
after ending the life of such a young girl.

21:22.270 --> 21:25.140
Should we kill him before leaving?

21:25.140 --> 21:26.250
You want to do it?

21:26.250 --> 21:28.760
No, we should kill as little as possible.

21:29.180 --> 21:33.210
We should go soon. Mr. Liebert 
will yell at us if we don't hurry.

21:33.210 --> 21:34.220
You're right.

21:52.350 --> 21:57.810
Even so, thank goodness his companion 
was already dead. It helped us out a lot.

21:57.810 --> 21:59.000
I agree.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 12

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Price of Betrayal and Price of Gold

23:45.780 --> 23:49.430
Next Episode: 
"Price of Betrayal and Price of Gold"
